Package: patrone-default-apps
Architecture: all
# Retiring Nautilus moved here from patrone-file-manager (0.3.11), files and
# diversions both, so the file manager installed on its own leaves it be. A
# package can't remove another's diversions: the file manager's 0.3.11 gives
# its own back when it's configured, which has to come before this package
# is unpacked and makes them again (preinst), hence Pre-Depends.
Pre-Depends: patrone-file-manager (>= 0.3.11)
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, patrone-browser-chooser
Recommends: patrone-notepad, patrone-terminal, patrone-unpack
Replaces: patrone-file-manager (<< 0.3.11)
Description: PatroneOS's default apps
 PatroneOS comes with no web browser: until one's installed, web links
 open Patrone Browser Chooser, which asks which one to install. Whichever
 browser is installed then opens them, and comes first in the favorites,
 with Patrone Terminal. Folders open in Patrone File Manager, which takes
 Ubuntu's Files' place in the favorites, archives, .deb packages and
 Flatpak files in Patrone Unpack, and plain text in Notepad. Users' own
 choices still win. GNOME's Files (Nautilus) stays installed, for other
 apps' file dialogs, but hidden, and "show in folder" opens Patrone File
 Manager.
